  "answer": "The Strength note now has an app on its App side. It walks you through the 4-week block one training day at a time.\n\n- **Today's session:** It opens on your next unfinished day. It shows each lift with its weight and sets × reps, and one big button per set that you tap to tick. A progress bar fills as you go.\n- **Navigation:** A plan overview lists weeks 1–4 with Mon, Wed and Fri buttons showing sets done out of total. Previous and Next buttons move between days.\n- **Where the data lives:** The 12 sessions, with their dates starting Mon 12 Oct, are in the app's own data. Your set ticks are saved there too. The note text hasn't changed.\n- **Weights:** Week 2 is +2.5 kg on every lift, and week 3 is +5 kg over week 1. Week 4 is a deload at the week 1 weights.\n\nI read \"2x5\" for week 4 as applying to every lift, so the deload deadlift and rows are also 2×5.\n\nThe final app check reported no problems except that no control sent an edit to the note. That's expected, because set ticks go to the app's data rather than the note.",
